 "queue": "it",
 "summary": "E013 Ethan Brooks (Engineering Intern) can't reach the internal wiki or the git repo when working from home on Fridays. He asked whether VPN is what he needs for remote access. A VPN access request has been filed for him (manager approval pending). Please confirm whether VPN is enough for the wiki and repo, or whether something else is needed, and help him troubleshoot if needed."
}

{
 "kind": "escalated",
 "message": "Hi Ethan! \ud83d\udc4b I've done two things:\n\n1. **Filed your VPN access request (REQ-1001).** It's gone to your manager, Marcus Webb, for approval. Under POL-ACC-01, VPN is a standard system, so the manager approves it, usually within 1 business day. You won't have access until Marcus approves it.\n\n2. **Sent your question to IT (ticket ESC-1002).** None of our policies say whether VPN is all you need to reach the wiki and the repo from home, so I can't promise it will fix the problem. IT will confirm whether VPN is enough or if you need something else, and they can help you troubleshoot.\n\nOn working from home: POL-REM-01 lets office-based employees work remotely up to 2 days a week if their manager agrees, so Fridays with Marcus's OK are fine.",
 "cited_policy_ids": [
  "POL-ACC-01",
  "POL-REM-01"
 ]
}
